; gh-ocannl-1652, gh-ocannl-1290, gh-ocannl-1688: type-checking stand-ins for the vendor binding
; packages, so the GPU backends and every vendor-gated `select` arm compile under `dune build
; @check` on every machine -- mac-studio and per-PR CI among them -- rather than only on a box
; carrying the vendor toolkit. `arrayjit/lib/cuda_backend.ml`, `hip_backend.ml` and
; `metal_backend.ml` live in `(optional)` libraries over `cudajit`/`hipjit`/`metal`, which dune skips
; SILENTLY wherever the package is absent, and the test and tool executables pick their vendor arm
; with a `select` that falls back to a stub just as silently, so before this a CUDA-only compile
; clash (gh-ocannl-1511) could merge unseen.
;
; Each package subdirectory (`cudajit`, `hipjit`, `metal`) holds:
;
; - a stub library (`cudajit_stub`, `hipjit_stub`, `metal_stub`) whose `.mli` files are VERBATIM
;   copies of the installed package's interfaces, never hand edits. They are kept out of `dune fmt`
;   (`.ocamlformat-ignore`). The library is interface-only (`modules_without_implementation`): it
;   type-checks and archives, and nothing can link it. Two files are hand-written, each because the
;   package installs no interface for it to copy: `hipjit/hip_ffi.mli`, the single type `hip.mli`
;   re-exports from hipjit's ctypes-generated `Hip_ffi`, which the compiler checks against that
;   re-export; and `metal/runtime.mli`, the part of `metal.runtime`'s inferred `Runtime` that
;   `metal.mli` and `metal_math_api_runtime.ml` use, which `runtest-runtime` checks the installed
;   `Runtime` against (`metal/dune` says how).
; - `typecheck/`, a library compiling `copy_files#` copies of the backend source and of the vendor
;   arm of `arrayjit.context`'s `select` (`<backend>_backend_impl.<package>.ml`) against the stub,
;   with the real backend's preprocessing and `arrayjit` libraries. Its errors name the original
;   `arrayjit/lib/` file and line. It is unwrapped, so the backend module has the top-level name the
;   arms below reach it by. Nothing links it; the real backend keeps linking the real package.
; - a `runtest-<module>` rule per stub interface (`runtest-cuda`, ...) checking it against the
;   installed package wherever that is installed (rog for cudajit, minix and tuf for hipjit -- the
;   daily sweep runs it there as part of `runtest` -- and every macOS build for metal), and a
;   SKIPPED line elsewhere. For a verbatim copy the check is a diff, which is the generator as well:
;   after a package upgrade on its box, the alias fails with the drift, and `dune promote` there
;   rewrites the copy from the installed interface.
;
; `arms/` then compiles the other vendor-gated `select` arms -- of the `arrayjit/test`,
; `test/operations` and `tools` executables -- as libraries against those stubs and `typecheck/`
; copies (`arms/dune` says how).
;
; What this proves is compilation against the interface, not behavior: the stub cannot catch a
; vendor-library change that keeps its signatures.
